{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792267225,"nonce":"T9PqoXijGMe2PgQKC6gS+z004eM=","title":"The Haxe heap per layout node is far above the objects' size, and grows faster than the node count","message":"**What**\n\nChimpMonk's editor (git-bug eb19594 there) measures the collected Haxe heap after a double Gc.major at each stage, built against ashui 5007496: ASH_GC_STATS=1 scripts/editor.sh --memory-probe in /Users/amaterasu/Vibranium/chimpmonk (editor/tests/MemoryProbe.hx).\n\n- The workspace shell, no scene: 37 to 41 MB at 129 layout nodes, about 285 KB a node.\n- Each tool panel alone: 0.2 to 1.6 MB. Opening all 16 at once adds 199 MB at 2652 nodes, where opening them one at a time sums to about 50 MB. So the cost grows faster than the node count when many panels are mounted together.\n- Closing leaves residue: the Project panel is +26 MB open and about 8.7 MB stays after close; all panels opened and closed leave about 15 MB more than before. A Viewport built alone and disposed keeps about 2 MB.\n\nRuled out on ChimpMonk's side: hidden panels (FloatingPanel unmounts them), icons (lazy), the GlyphAtlas and ImageAtlas Haxe bytes (upload scratch).\n\n**Suspects**\n\nNot confirmed without a typed census: a per-node CSS cascade or computed-style cache, registries keyed by node that outlive disposal (Identity, Interaction, Scroll), Watch.bySlot entries, per-element closures.\n\n**Next**\n\nA typed heap census, which ChimpMonk asked the Ash session for (report-gc: Ash owns the heap tooling). Then reproduce in ashui alone with a tree of a few thousand nodes built and disposed, and read each registry's size before and after. Related: d6a0e46 and d701ddf.","files":null}]}